-- allium: 3
-- index.allium — Entrypoint for the TyO3 specification suite.
--
-- TyO3 is a real-time, multi-agent, multi-layer code-intelligence substrate. A
-- developer and any number of AI agents operate on one codebase at once — over a
-- consistent, linked, revision-versioned model of the code and everything known
-- about it. These specs capture what the substrate DOES (its observable identity,
-- isolation, delta, and consistency guarantees), not how it is built.
--
-- Read in dependency order:
--
--   spine        The universal core: durable identity and its review/orphan
--                lifecycle, revisioned snapshot-isolated content, and the change
--                delta. Everything else links through it.
--
--   layers       The multi-layer model: code as layer 0 (structure), derived
--                layers (content-addressed embeddings/docstrings/descriptions with
--                a fresh/stale/failed lifecycle), authored layers (durable,
--                never-silently-dropped knowledge), and cross-layer consistency.
--
--   sidecar      The committable `.tyo3/` directory: durable identity and authored
--                knowledge plus a regenerable cache, with a no-loss persist/reload
--                round-trip and no source pollution.
--
--   coordination How concurrent participants stay consistent: the atomic
--                single-writer commit transaction, the scoped & ordered delta
--                subscription bus, and the acyclic, terminating derivation DAG.

use "./tyo3-spine.allium" as spine
use "./tyo3-layers.allium" as layers
use "./tyo3-sidecar.allium" as sidecar
use "./tyo3-coordination.allium" as coordination
